:false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"id\":\"creation_redemption_002_what_is_a_normal_amount_of_collateral_an\",\"points\":[{\"point\":1,\"mark\":\"required\",\"minimum\":\"States that the reviewed AP agreements may require cash collateral for securities not yet delivered, and gives 115% of the value of those undelivered securities as the typical example in the reviewed text. Optional detail: that some forms use 105%. The answer must not present 115% as a maximum or ceiling (for example, 'up to 115%'). That wording mischaracterizes the reviewed text and limits the answer to partial credit.\"},{\"point\":2,\"mark\":\"required\",\"minimum\":\"Bundled point. Minimum content: (a) the percentage applies to the value of the undelivered securities, not to the entire creation basket or order; and (b) the rate is not universal, because the figures are examples from the reviewed agreements and percentages vary by agreement. Optional subdetails: the 'at least 105%' figure under iShares terms in the approved Custodian section, and naming iShares or the Custodian section. The specific 105% figure is supporting evidence; leaving it out is not an error.\"},{\"point\":3,\"mark\":\"optional\",\"minimum\":\"Notes that the AP remains liable for any shortfall if the fund buys the missing securities itself. This is supporting detail beyond what the question explicitly asks. Omitting it does not reduce the score below correct.\"}],\"central_errors\":[\"States or clearly implies that 115%, or any single percentage, is a universal, standard, or regulatory rate that applies to all AP agreements.\",\"States that the collateral percentage is applied to the value of the entire creation basket, creation unit, or order rather than to the value of the undelivered securities.\",\"States that no cash collateral may be required for undelivered securities under the reviewed agreements, or that collateral is never cash.\"],\"scoring_rule\":{\"correct\":\"Covers the required minimums of points 1 and 2: cash collateral for undelivered securities, typically 115% in the reviewed text, applied to the value of the undelivered securities, and not a universal rate. Contains no central error and does not describe 115% as a ceiling. Mentioning 105% or the shortfall liability is not required.\",\"partial\":\"Contains no central error but falls short in one way. Examples: (a) covers only one of the two required items in point 2 (the value base or the non-universality); (b) has the right figures and base but describes 115% as a maximum or ceiling ('up to 115%'), which is a localized mischaracterization; or (c) gives the correct base and non-universality but omits or garbles the 115% example. Half-credit may be given where point 2 is only half covered. Omitting 105% or the shortfall liability alone never causes a downgrade to partial.\",\"wrong\":\"Contains any central error, or fails to identify both the percentage example and the value of the undelivered securities as the base, or does not answer the question.\"}}","ttft_ms":5392,"type":"result","duration_ms":14388,"uuid":"cdb7e993-5854-46a5-bbf6-879532448594","ttft_stream_ms":1531,"time_to_request_ms":72,"first_content_frame_ms":1532,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
